# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output — never committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
build
.build
.swiftpm
Derived/
*.xcresult

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated Xcode projects.
#
# RULE: a generated project is committed ONLY where it sits on the documented USER path.
#
#   Examples/  -> COMMITTED. `Scripts/verify_capture.sh` is the documented one-command
#                 verification, and its behaviour when the project is absent is: regenerate if
#                 `xcodegen` is on PATH, otherwise `die` with "Install XcodeGen (brew install
#                 xcodegen)". Requiring a separate install before the headline command works
#                 would contradict the drop-in promise, so the project ships.
#   Research/  -> IGNORED. That harness is a maintainer tool; its README documents the one-line
#                 `xcodegen generate`.
#
# The drift risk that comes with committing generated output is handled by CI (regenerate and
# require an empty diff), not by withholding the file.
#
# Note the negations are load-bearing and must stay: `*.xcworkspace` also matches
# `ScreenGuardDemo.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace`, which is part of the .xcodeproj bundle and is
# required for Xcode to open the project at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace
!Examples/**/*.xcodeproj
!Examples/**/*.xcworkspace

# Per-user Xcode state, written whenever the project is opened or built. Machine-specific, churns
# constantly, and means nothing to anyone else.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored: `<project>.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/xcschemes/*.xcscheme`. Those are
# shared, and they are what makes `xcodebuild -scheme ScreenGuardDemo` work on a fresh clone
# without opening Xcode first so it auto-creates a user scheme — which the documented one-command
# verification depends on. Ignoring xcuserdata/ does not affect them.
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcuserdatad

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AgentTeams runtime state.
#
# Task graph, mailboxes, attempt ids and progress for the team session that built this repository.
# Tool-managed, machine- and session-specific, and rewritten continuously while a team runs — so
# committing it would produce churn and conflicts with no product value. Everything it produced
# that matters was distilled into `docs/evidence/` and the amendment ledger in
# `docs/api-contract.md` §13, so no finding lives only here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.agent-teams/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Measurement artifacts.
#
# Raw output of the capture-matrix harness (PNGs, logs, JSON) — regenerable with
# `Research/Scripts/capture_matrix.sh`. Only the canonical runs cited by
# `docs/evidence/capability-matrix.md` §1 are committed, so every number in that document has its
# raw evidence in the repository, without carrying every experiment ever run (12 MB -> ~3.3 MB).
#
# The parent directory must stay trackable for the negations to work: git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Research/Artifacts/*
!Research/Artifacts/20261002-151754-matrix/
!Research/Artifacts/20261002-151341-feasibility/
!Research/Artifacts/20261002-151448-replayKit/
!Research/Artifacts/20261002-153117-renderSanity/
